  "foaf:name": "Coastal Sargassum Interception and Regeneration",
  "sdo:name": "Coastal Sargassum Interception and Regeneration",
  "sdo:description": "Coastal Sargassum Interception and Regeneration is a solutions-oriented Decade Project addressing recurrent sargassum influxes along tropical coastlines. It focuses on early interception near-shore or upon landing to prevent anaerobic decay, methane emissions, and coastal damage. Intercepted biomass undergoes low-impact, science-informed bioremediation to neutralize excess salinity and heavy metals, enabling safe conversion into regenerative outputs such as biochar-enriched compost for soil restoration and local livelihoods. Implemented initially in sargassum-affected regions, the project delivers scalable ocean-based solutions aligned with the Global Ecosystem for Ocean Solutions (GEOS) Programme.",
  "sdo:location": "Monaco",
  "sdo:identifier": "72.1",
  "sdo:url": "https://oceandecade.org/actions/coastal-sargassum-interception-and-regeneration/",
